{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/512122-courts-of-tales-help-please","id":512122,"title":"Courts of tales-help please","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-12T10:43:40-07:00","id":512122,"title":"Courts of tales-help please","content":"For my campaign, we're making four Courts based on fairy tales. But I have problem how to develop them, especially where they would rule and contracts. Could you help me?<br /> <br /> Here is first:<br /> <br /> Court of Mirrors-Court of Pride,Translucent Court, Beautiful Trap<br /> <br /> Court was founded by Snow White. 'King' was actually True Fae, who kiddnaped her mother, making her Fairest Romancer. She fell in love with him, poor soul, and it didn't matter that he kiddnaped her from hands of her fiance, from her native Japan, forcing her into ultimate servitude as European themed Queen. But soon, as all changelings, she found herself infertile...but Kings need heirs. She called upon long forgotten Contract to become pregnant, then made Contracts with blood, snow and ebony, to shape child to her desires. With another slave, she conceived child, too twisted in Fairest. But kithless, she was overlooked, till her 7th year, when she was more beautiful than Loyalist Queen. Queen ordered her death, but hunter spared girl and she ran, run through 14 other Realms, Realms of mound and sea, till she escaped to Hedge. there, she found refuge with '7 dwarves'- Miner, Smith, Earthbones, Metalflesh, hobgoblin, Fetch and Ensorcelled.<br /> But wicked Queen found girl, and thrice poisoned her, each time with new tactic, years apart. Till Summer Prince found girl. Together, they rejoiced as wicked Queen fell, dying dancing in iron shoes. And Snow White went and claimed her mirror, greatest of them all, and threatened to shatter it, till Mirror didn't accept her Contract. Then she called upon Pride, and they had contest in boasting-and Snow White won.<br /> This Court's colours are white, black and red. Their symbol is mirror, surrounded by frozen apple-bearing ebony, woven with ribbons, pierced by comb. They bow to no one, and subtly manipulate everybody. They believe that their self-worth must be preserved, and that everybody has something good about themselves. All members of this Court are arrogant to bone, and to hold standing in Court, they must show what they flatter themselves.<br /> Court's mantle manifests as light and images reflected on changeling's skin, projecting aura of confidence.<br /> Now, I need help with Contracts and where or when it would rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6005,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","user":"coolcat12345","date":". 05-12-2015, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:32:04-07:00","id":512212,"title":"","content":"If you want to follow the model of the Seasons, the structure for Contracts would probably be a &quot;Fleeting&quot; Contract dealing with the Court emotion(Pride, in this case) and one dealing with the Court's thematics. Less sure how to work this, since Mirrors and Vainglory already cover that sort of space.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, I can't really tell in a vacuum. What are the other Courts like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T05:17:44-07:00","id":512834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/512122-courts-of-tales-help-please?p=512212#post512212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to follow the model of the Seasons, the structure for Contracts would probably be a &quot;Fleeting&quot; Contract dealing with the Court emotion(Pride, in this case) and one dealing with the Court's thematics. Less sure how to work this, since Mirrors and Vainglory already cover that sort of space.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, I can't really tell in a vacuum. What are the other Courts like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think one Contract is enough. Thanks for help!<br /> <br /> Other:<br /> __________________________________________________ __________________________________________________ __________________________________________________ ___________<br /> <br /> Court of Briars-Court of Love, Rosy Court, Dreaming Spindle<br /> Founded by Talia, also known as Briar Rose or Sleeping Beauty. Once upon a time, two Gentry had special Feud-they would fight, to see who was more beloved by humans. They aided now long lost kingdom, that was where is now Italy, for milleniums. But one of them became sloppy, spending less time as Carabosse, her Actor, and more as Forgotten Tower, her Realm. She thought that making Queen fertile, in form of frog, was thing Lilac Fairy could never outmatch. But she came, with 6 wisp-the Dedaly Dancers-and gifted gifts to Princess. Carabosse, enraged, cursed princess with death-thinking fear will make everybody love her. Lilac undone it. Just for Carabosse to assume form of spindle, and drive human woman insane, so she won't hear desclaimer of spindles being illegal. When princess pricked finger, Carabosse pulled castle in hedge, but after Lilac made everybody asleep. Talia fought, and became best oneiromancer ever, diving through dreams, drawing people forth, till son of local Freehold's ruler's didn't come forth. Seizing her chance, Lilac parted Hedge-and as 100 years passed, she won Feud. Some mention rape, but so far, those are just rumors.Prince and Fairest Flowering Talia was now went away. Prince's Gristlegrinder mother was changeling of those 2 Fae-some say she thought Briar Rose, as she called herself now, Loyalist-others say she was one herself. Whatever story, she tried to eat newborn children, her own grandchildren. She failed, and met gruesome fate herself. Rpse, who mastered Hedge, made Contract with briars-not place, but element, of course.<br /> Court's colours are rose pink, dark red and shadowy green. It's symbol is vine, whose thorns grow in spindles, and whose roses have eye at center. They believe that love, something Gentry cannot conceive, will keep them protected. Dreamy and dramatic, they are wild and unstoppable. In this Court, more you fight for what you love, higher you rise.<br /> Mantle manifests as sharp nails, rosy skin, and aromatic, dark smokes. It invokes sympathy in others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T02:06:10-07:00","id":590036,"title":"","content":"Court of Bones-Court of Content, Teal Court, Flaming Skull.<br /> Founded by Vasilisa the Beautiful. When she was young, her stepfamily threw her out in Hedge, to seek Baba Yaga. hag's origin is lost-some say she was first of what would become Witchtooth and Antiquarian, some call her Hobgoblin, Some say she was Transcended True Fae, and some call her embodiment of Wyrd itself. Whatever she was, Vasilisa worked for her, with help of special Token-doll containing her dead mother's will. There, Vasilisa struck Contracts with morning,noon,evening and Sun. She came home, as Flamesiren, and burned her stepfamily to ashes. She became friend with Witchtooth of Night court, and married Tsar of Day. But it wasn't enough, and she broke her connection with them, instead forming her own Court.]<br /> Court's colours are teal, bone greay and silver. It's symbol is kull with green and orange flames, and doll in it's mouth, surrounded by ribbons and things Vasilisa struck contract with. They live by legend that Gentry struck bargains with all emotions but one-content-and that it will protect them. They are happy with what they have, and patient and calm. More you wait and work, and less complain, more you rise.<br /> mantle manifests as bony head and dust over body, flames dancing in hair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T20:00:03-07:00","id":590718,"title":"","content":"Is this going to be Changeling 1e or 2e? Because for 2e there is a dev post on creating courts and a sample Toronto Freehold with the Courts of Brass, Ivory, Jade, Silver as example courts. The guidelines are very good. Heck even for a 1e game it all kinds of ideas you could pillage.<br /> <br /> Example Your Court of Pride could have contract of emotion (Pride) using fleeting contract of spring, replacing desire with Pride, instead of Talespinning Contracts just use the Contract of Dreams (because I have no idea what the Talespinning contract looks like), and pick a thematic set of contracts from an existing Contract like Vainglory. The design the Court Mantle, but replace the 4th dots effect with some other bonus. If we're talking 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T04:27:11-07:00","id":591099,"title":"","content":"We are talking about 1ed. Thank you-I have much problems with mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}